 would love this feature","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4531243661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4651686237","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101473#issuecomment-4651686237","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101473","id":4651686237,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFUMZXQ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-08T17:35:22Z","updated_at":"2026-06-08T17:35:22Z","body":"> Having this same issue and would love this feature\r\n\r\n@trevorbaughn As per the above comment:\r\n\r\n> I would also like to see an example of a real-world case where it would help.\r\n\r\nCould you describe a concrete use case where you need this? This would help us better assess whether this PR should be merged.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4651686237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4871175046","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101473#issuecomment-4871175046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101473","id":4871175046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIlg7hg","user":{"login":"teaganbaughn","id":36556547,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NTU2NTQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36556547?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn","html_url":"https://github.com/teaganbaughn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teaganbaughn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-02T23:06:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T23:06:11Z","body":"> > Having this same issue and would love this feature\r\n> \r\n> @trevorbaughn As per the above comment:\r\n> \r\n> > I would also like to see an example of a real-world case where it would help.\r\n> \r\n> Could you describe a concrete use case where you need this? This would help us better assess whether this PR should be merged.\r\n\r\nIf I remember correctly;\r\n\r\nTurns out there's some weird stuff you can do by enabling editable children and disabling it that leaves the boolean set (for some reason?).  Seems like a bug, but I am using it as my team's environment artist has created a complex mesh that does not seem to get it's faces correctly imported (and no matter which way I look, online or otherwise, I can't seem to figure this out - it seems fine in Blender).  This led to our player character falling through walls and floors at times that seem rather random to me.  The solution to that problem was to enable backface collisions - itself not an ideal solution, but simply being able to do that in the importer would remove the need to make children editable - as described in the proposal linked at the top of this thread.\r\n\r\nSending this thread to the artist in question.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4871175046/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]